# SyncOffset Release Discipline (Web)

## System Auditor gate (overrides “done”)

Per **syncoffset-system-auditor.mdc**:

- No feature work may be considered **complete** until the System Auditor reports **PASS** or **WARN** only on the post-task **SYSTEM HEALTH REPORT**.
- Any **CRITICAL** finding (git topology, schema drift, RLS, dependency corruption, wrong repo commit) **automatically reopens** the task.
- Pre-work audit is mandatory before implementation.

## Database rules

- Web migrations live in `syncoffset-web/supabase/migrations/`.
- Schedule migrations require **mobile** `20260519000000_production_documents_layer.sql` applied on the target DB first (FK dependency).
- Constitutional `documents` requires legacy rename per `docs/SYNCOFFSET_SCHEMA_DECISION_RECORD.md` before `20260531000100`.

## Git rules

- Confirm `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` is **syncoffset-web** before committing web work.
- Mobile Expo changes belong in **syncoffset-mobile**, not this repo.
- Stage intentional paths only; verify `git status` file counts before commit.

## Production protection

Without explicit user approval, NEVER execute production SQL, deploy production migrations, or modify production data.

## Task completion

The **SYSTEM HEALTH REPORT** from the System Auditor is required at task end. **FAIL** or **CRITICAL** blocks completion.
